# VTID-03961 — commands run during this change

## Why (context confirmed live before writing any code)

Immediately after merging VTID-03958 (PR #3346, env_overrides input), checked
what dispatching AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml with env_overrides would
actually ship, per CLAUDE.md's Part 1 IF-THEN rule 26 ("pin/scope a
session-approved prod deploy to this session's own change, not whatever else
is on staging/main"):

$ aws ecs describe-task-definition --task-definition vitana-gateway-awsdr:103 \
    --region eu-central-1 \
    --query 'taskDefinition.containerDefinitions[0].environment[?name==`GIT_COMMIT_SHA`||name==`BUILD_INFO_MARKER`]'
  GIT_COMMIT_SHA=dc2d17d210678522e973a1bc94453f153eb39e5b

$ curl -s https://gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/admin/build-info
  {"env":"production","git_commit":"dc2d17d2...","booted_at":"2026-09-15T14:53:00Z"}
$ curl -s https://preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com/api/v1/admin/build-info
  {"env":"staging","git_commit":"7b9ca15b...","booted_at":"2026-09-16T12:19:22Z"}

$ git log --oneline dc2d17d210678522e973a1bc94453f153eb39e5b..7b9ca15b41c8dbb89d1ec41ac68b2d5da0ae59f6
  30 commits, including VTID-03932 (Commerce Partner Onboarding), VTID-03894
  (supplier self-service catalogue), an Aurora/Cognito cutover merge, and
  more — none discussed or approved as part of enabling the on-ramp flag.

Both existing `deploy_mode`s (promote-staging, rebuild-main) always
re-derive the shipped image from staging's or main's current HEAD — neither
can express "ship literally nothing code-wise, just a task-def env var".
Presented this finding to the platform owner with two options (build a
narrow env-only mode vs. accept a full staging promotion); owner chose the
narrow mode.

## Fix

.github/workflows/AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml:
  1. Header comment: "Two modes" -> "Three modes", documents env-only and
     why it exists (references this VTID and CLAUDE.md IF-THEN rule 26).
  2. `deploy_mode` input: added `env-only` to the existing `options` list
     (a CHOICE VALUE on the already-existing input — does NOT add a new
     workflow_dispatch input; count stays 24, confirmed below).
  3. "Resolve deploy source" step: new FIRST branch, `if [ "$DEPLOY_MODE" =
     "env-only" ]`. Reads the CURRENT `ECS_SERVICE` task definition's own
     image and GIT_COMMIT_SHA (aws ecs describe-services ->
     describe-task-definition) and echoes them back as this run's
     `mode`/`image`/`sha`/`short` outputs, then `exit 0` BEFORE the
     promote-staging section's staging build-info curl or the
     rebuild-main branch — env-only never touches staging or main at all.
     Fails loudly (::error::, non-zero exit) if the current image can't be
     resolved; falls back to sha="unknown" (not a crash) if
     GIT_COMMIT_SHA is absent from the current task def.
  4. Because "Build task-definition (1/2)" always rewrites
     `.containerDefinitions[0].image` and the GIT_COMMIT_SHA/COMMIT_SHA/
     BUILD_INFO_MARKER env vars from `steps.source.outputs.*`, and env-only
     mode sets those outputs to the CURRENT live values, that rewrite is a
     byte-for-byte no-op under env-only — no code change needed there. Only
     step "(2/2)"'s env_overrides (or another dispatch-input override)
     block can change anything under this mode.

## New tests

services/gateway/test/vtid-03961-env-only-deploy-mode.test.ts (7 tests):
  - deploy_mode still has exactly the expected 3 options; input COUNT
    unchanged at 24 (a choice value, not a new input)
  - extracts the REAL "Resolve deploy source" step script (not a
    reimplementation), confirms bash -n passes on it standalone
  - env-only's branch calls describe-services/describe-task-definition and
    returns before the promote-staging section's STAGING_URL curl is ever
    reached (string-position assertion on the real script)
  - executes the real extracted script under a stub `aws` on PATH:
    echoes back the current image/commit unchanged; falls back to
    sha="unknown" when GIT_COMMIT_SHA is absent; fails loudly
    (non-zero exit + ::error::) when the current image can't be resolved
  - rebuild-main mode's branch is unaffected (still selects mode=rebuild-main)

Iteration note: the first draft of the harness ran the extracted script
without sanitizing GitHub's `${{ ... }}` template syntax, which is not
valid bash on its own ("bad substitution") — fixed by blanking those
expressions before execution (the stub `aws` only pattern-matches on
subcommand text, not flag values, so this is a safe stand-in for GitHub's
real interpolation). A second early failure (checking `result.stderr` for
the `::error::` line) was fixed by also checking stdout — the script's
`::error::` lines are plain `echo` (matching every other override block's
convention in this file), not `>&2`.

